<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">White Terror (Hungary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The White Terror in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was a wave of counter-revolutionary violence in 1919–1921 after the fall of the Hungarian Soviet Republic. Officer detachments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy">Miklós Horthy</a>'s National Army killed, imprisoned and tortured thousands of suspected communists, socialists and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. Many opponents fled abroad, some to the Serbian-occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baranya">Baranya</a> region, and the violence accompanied Horthy's rise to regent in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/white-terror-hungary.jpg" alt="White Terror (Hungary)" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author; photo from the Photo Archive of the Hungarian National Museum · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Execution_in_Tab.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
